# Every OS checks out each file byte for byte as git stores it: no end-of-line conversion, ever (M1-06).
# Git for Windows, and so GitHub's Windows runners, turn LF into CRLF on checkout by default, and then the snapshot
# and fixture tests, which compare bytes, fail on Windows only. Files are written with LF; prettier, rustfmt and ruff
# keep them that way. Nothing is marked as text, so a binary fixture is never altered either.
* -text

# Golden protobuf messages are compared byte for byte, so git never treats them as text: no line-ending
# conversion on any checkout (an autocrlf clone, the Windows CI job) and no text diffs.
*.binpb binary

# The event-log fixtures are frames of protobuf bytes (contracts 7.1), compared byte for byte: binary, no text diffs.
fixtures/event-logs/*.log binary
